Say why a candidate personality is dropped before it is instantiated

The panel shows M<n> from probeCandidates and not one "nio: C" line, and
"nio: C" is printed in the second loop of that function, so the second loop
never runs: every personality is turned away by the first one.  The first
loop has eight doors and this records which one each candidate is turned
away at, so the panel names the door instead of leaving it to guesswork.

The line is printed only for the nubs that dropped every candidate, which is
the symptom, so the nubs that match normally stay quiet.  Reason 6 (the kext
that holds the personality has not been loaded) also gets a line of its own,
naming the kext that is missing.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index df38670..bfc0ad8 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
